{
 "_file": "data/pcm-2020-family.json",
 "_what": "Single vs companion, and a theme group, for every plate in the PCM 2020 design book. SOURCE, not output: scripts/pcm_extract.py reads it and must never overwrite it.",
 "_why": [
  "The 2020 book prints no section headings at all -- no Individual/Companion split",
  "and no themes -- so extract_2020() had only the plate's aspect ratio to go on and",
  "filed every companion under \"Flat Markers\". Once the catalog page groups designs",
  "by what a family is shopping for (one name / two names) rather than by which book",
  "the plate came out of, that guess is load-bearing and had to be replaced with a",
  "real reading of each plate."
 ],
 "_provenance": [
  "family: HAND-CLASSIFIED BY LOOKING, 2026-08-15 (sprint-23 Track D). All 354",
  "plates were rendered into 24 contact sheets at 480x274 per plate",
  "(scratch/s23d_family_sheets.py) and read one sheet at a time. A plate is",
  "\"companion\" when the art carries two or more person blocks -- two given names,",
  "each with its own dates. It is \"single\" when it carries one name, INCLUDING the",
  "common layout of one name with two flanking date boxes (born / died), which is",
  "the shape most easily mistaken for a companion. Judgement calls are listed under",
  "_ambiguous with the reasoning.",
  "The method was validated against the 2011 book first: the two proof manifests",
  "agree with that book's own printed Individual/Companion split on 330 of 330",
  "numbers they cover (119 companions in pcm-companion-proofs, 0 in singles; 211",
  "individuals in pcm-single-proofs, 0 in companions). No 2020 number appears in",
  "either manifest, so the 2020 book had no such cross-check and had to be read.",
  "",
  "theme: DERIVED from data/pcm-subject-tags.json by the ordered rule table in",
  "scratch/s23d_build_family.py, with the hand overrides listed there. The tags are",
  "themselves a by-looking file; the derivation is deterministic so it can be",
  "re-run and argued with. fmt == \"ledger\" short-circuits to the Ledgers group,",
  "matching how the 2011 book files its six companion ledgers."
 ],
 "_values": {
  "family": [
   "single",
   "companion"
  ],
  "theme": [
   "Classic",
   "Religious",
   "Outdoors",
   "Floral",
   "Misc",
   "Child",
   "Ledgers"
  ]
 },
 "_ambiguous": {
  "675": "companion: two people stacked rather than side by side (a father block and a daughter block), each with its own name and date pair.",
  "711": "companion: two separate name banners with different surnames and one date pair each; the art is a parent-and-child silhouette, not a spousal pair.",
  "775": "companion: two given names share one surname line (\"BRODY & ANDY\") and the plate carries two date ranges. Brothers, not spouses.",
  "872": "companion: a Mother block and a Father block stacked, each a full name with its own dates.",
  "961": "companion: FOUR names in two book panels. Neither a one-name marker nor strictly a two-name one; filed with the multi-name designs because a family shopping the Single section is shopping for one name.",
  "992": "companion: \"Susan & Charlie\" set as one display line over two date pairs, so the second given name reads as ornament until the dates are counted."
 },
